; bal -V --unrealized --anon keeps the revaluation between postings and
; foots as it did before the balance report valued postings at cost.
; anonymize_posts relabels a posting's cost and the price in its lot
; annotation separately and gives the dollar two labels: print --anon
; shows the lot as "10 A {=C150.00}" and the books as "B10.00".  A cost
; baseline would read the lot's cost in B while the report values the lot
; at its fixated price in C, and the report total would be "B1500.00 /
; C-1500.00".  Account names are hashed at random under --anon, so each
; report prints its total only.

2024/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL {=$150}
    Assets:Checking

2024/01/15 Books
    Expenses:Books          $10.00
    Assets:Checking

test bal -V --unrealized --anon --balance-format '%/%(scrub(display_total))\n' --now 2024/04/01
0
end test

test bal --exchange $ --unrealized --anon --balance-format '%/%(scrub(display_total))\n' --now 2024/04/01
0
end test
